# Line-ending policy.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a per-machine setting and is not cloned, so the repository
# cannot rely on it: two contributors could produce different bytes for the
# same file. These attributes are versioned, so the rule applies everywhere.
#
# The history already stores LF throughout, so this only pins what is there.

# Normalize to LF in the repository, and keep the working tree LF on every
# platform too — that is what makes a checkout byte-identical across machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception. cmd.exe is documented to misparse
# LF-only scripts around labels and multi-line blocks, and the dev shims in
# bin/ use multi-line `if` blocks, so they keep CRLF on disk.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never let text conversion run over binary assets. `text=auto` already detects
# these correctly; stating it explicitly keeps the intent visible. Add further
# asset types here as they appear.
*.png binary
